        ": سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنِ اَلْمَرْأَةِ تَقْضِي شَهْرَ رَمَضَانَ فَيُكْرِهُهَا زَوْجُهَا عَلَى اَلْإِفْطَارِ فَقَالَ «لاَ يَنْبَغِي أَنْ يُكْرِهَهَا بَعْدَ زَوَالِ اَلشَّمْسِ»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2001 - Sama‘ah narrated from Abu Basir, who said: I asked Abu ‘Abd Allah (as) about a woman making up missed fasts from Month of Ramadan, and her husband compels her to break her fast.\nImam (as) said: \"It is not appropriate for him to compel her to break her fast after the sun has passed its zenith.\""
        ]
      }
